Hello again,

as nobody has replied to my mail I tried out some things in the 
meanwhile:

I compiled the 2.4.25 kernel (unpatched, only a little bug in mm/
filemap.c is fixed). There are no ACPI error messages. (Some time ago I 
tried kernel 2.4.26-rc2 (unpatched): it has the error messages.)
And again: 2.4.26 patched with the latest release of acpi (released on 
2004-05-24) shows the error messages, too.

The configuration files of the kernels (2.4.25 and 2.4.26-acpi) and the 
outputs of acpidmp, lspci -vv, dmidecode, dmesg, ... are attached. 
Perhaps it helps!?

Before I forget it again: My BIOS revision is 1005. (Should be in the 
output of dmidecode, too.)

Could anybody give me a hint how to handle these messages, please? I 
have no idea what they mean, if I can ignore them, or if I better 
should not use ACPI with the kernel.

Regards,
Christian Schneider

